' This is the canonical message passing diagram for the setup ceremony. An Ascii output without the notes should be placed inside the SPEC file.
@startuml setup_diagram_without_states
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title Setup Sequence Diagram (Without States)
box "User Side" #AliceBlue
actor User order 1 #LightCyan
participant Iso order 2 #LightBlue
participant Boomlet order 3 #LightPink
participant ST order 4 #Violet
participant Boomletwo order 4 #LightGray
participant Niso order 5 #LightGreen
participant Phone order 6 #CadetBlue
end box
participant WT order 98 #Red
participant SAR order 99 #Yellow
actor Peers order 100

autonumber "<b>[00]"
note over User:  **User** \n <i>milestone_block_collection: Collection<milestone_block> \n <i>wt_ids_collection: Collection<wt_id> [Identity of all agreed upon WT candidates, first is the one first attempted to activate] \n <i>sar_id: SarId [Identity of the peer's selected SAR] \n <i>network \n <i>entropy_bytes \n <i>passphrase \n <i>static_doxing_data \n <i>doxing_password \n <i>rpc_client_url \n <i>rpc_client_auth
/ note over WT:  **WT** \n <i>wt_privkey \n <i>wt_id: {\n <i>    wt_tor_address,\n <i>    wt_pubkey \n}\n <i>most_work_bitcoin_block_height
/ note over SAR:  **SAR** \n <i>sar_privkey \n <i>sar_id: {\n <i>    sar_tor_address,\n <i>    sar_pubkey \n <i>}\n
/ note over Phone:  **Phone** \n <i>dynamic_doxing_data
note over ST:  **ST** \n <i>DURESS_DISPLAY_VOCABULARY
note over User, SAR
<b>PARAMETERS
# #define PROTOCOL_VERSION
# #define MAX_TRIES_FOR_DIGGING_GAME_IN_BLOCKS
# #define MIN_TRIES_FOR_DIGGING_GAME_IN_BLOCKS
end note
group SAR sign-up

' Step 1
User o-> Phone:  <b>SetupPhoneInput1 \n doxing_password \n sar_id \n static_doxing_data
hnote over Phone #LavenderBlush:  Phone receives {doxing_password, sar_id, static_doxing_data} from User. The single SarId contains the selected SAR's Tor address and public key. \n StaticDoxingData contains the user's name, national ID, home and work addresses, mobile, home, and work phone numbers, and a trusted person's name, address, and phone number. \n DynamicDoxingData contains a schema identifier, capture time, and payload such as location. Phone NFC-normalizes doxing_password and encodes it as UTF-8 bytes, then saves doxing_key as \n tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key", doxing_password_bytes). It takes sar_pubkey from sar_id, obtains its canonical public-key bytes, derives doxing_key_for_sar as \n tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key_for_sar", doxing_key || sar_pubkey_bytes), and derives doxing_data_identifier as tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_data_identifier", doxing_key_for_sar). \n That SAR-specific key encrypts the user's static and dynamic doxing data, and the identifier initializes the SAR registration.
hnote over Phone #Lavender:  doxing_password_bytes := utf8(doxing_password) \n doxing_key := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key", doxing_password_bytes) \n sar_pubkey := sar_id.sar_pubkey \n sar_pubkey_bytes := canonical_public_key_bytes(sar_pubkey) \n doxing_key_for_sar := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key_for_sar", doxing_key || sar_pubkey_bytes) \n doxing_data_identifier := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_data_identifier", doxing_key_for_sar)

' Step 2
Phone o-> SAR:  <b>SetupPhoneSarMessage1 \n doxing_data_identifier
hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  SAR receives doxing_data_identifier from Phone, generates a service-fee invoice for this registration, sets its payment deadline, and creates SarServiceFeePaymentInfo containing that invoice, \n deadline, and the SAR's configured SarId. It retains the identifier as the lookup key for this pending registration and returns the payment information to Phone.
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  service_fee_invoice := invoice bound to doxing_data_identifier \n payment_deadline := deadline for service_fee_invoice \n sar_service_fee_payment_info := SarServiceFeePaymentInfo{ \n service_fee_invoice: service_fee_invoice, \n payment_deadline: payment_deadline, \n sar_id: sar_id \n}.

' Step 3
SAR o-> Phone:  <b>SetupSarPhoneMessage1 \n sar_service_fee_payment_info
hnote over Phone #LavenderBlush:  Phone receives sar_service_fee_payment_info from SAR, checks that its SarId equals the selected sar_id, and forwards it to User.
hnote over Phone #Pink:  Assert sar_service_fee_payment_info.sar_id == sar_id

' Step 4
Phone o-> User:  <b>SetupPhoneOutput1 \n sar_service_fee_payment_info
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives sar_service_fee_payment_info from Phone, verifies its SAR identity, invoice, and deadline, and pays it. Each resulting ServicePaymentReceipt contains the service identifier, invoice reference, and payment proof. \n User inputs the SAR payment receipts back to Phone.
hnote over User #Lavender:  sar_service_fee_payment_receipts := pay(sar_service_fee_payment_info)

' Step 5
User o-> Phone:  <b>SetupPhoneInput2 \n sar_service_fee_payment_receipts
hnote over Phone #LavenderBlush:  Phone receives sar_service_fee_payment_receipts from User. For static and dynamic data it derives separate CBC and CMAC keys from doxing_key_for_sar with "Boomerang/sar_stored_data". \n It encrypts static_doxing_data with canonical context {"sar_static_data", doxing_data_identifier} and dynamic_doxing_data with context \n {"sar_dynamic_data", doxing_data_identifier}. cbc_cmac_encrypt produces a CbcCmacEnvelope containing version, IV, ciphertext, and authentication tag. \n Phone sends the static envelope once and sends updated dynamic envelopes at intervals, each accompanied by the unauthenticated doxing_data_identifier lookup key and the payment receipts.
hnote over Phone #Lavender:  static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: derive_cbc_cmac_keys(doxing_key_for_sar, "Boomerang/sar_stored_data"), context: canonical_encode("sar_static_data", doxing_data_identifier), content: static_doxing_data) \n dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar := cbc_cmac_encrypt(keys: derive_cbc_cmac_keys(doxing_key_for_sar, "Boomerang/sar_stored_data"), context: canonical_encode("sar_dynamic_data", doxing_data_identifier), content: dynamic_doxing_data) \n note that static data is sent once and dynamic data is updated and sent in intervals \n Phone sends doxing_data_identifier alongside every sent message as an unauthenticated lookup identifier.

' Step 6
Phone o-> SAR:  <b>SetupPhoneSarMessage2 \n sar_service_fee_payment_receipts \n static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar \n doxing_data_identifier \n dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar [sent_at_intervals]
hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  SAR receives {sar_service_fee_payment_receipts, static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar, doxing_data_identifier, \n dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar} from Phone. It requires verify_payment to succeed and the identifier to equal the value received during initialization. \n It stores the encrypted static and dynamic data under that identifier and confirms synchronization. Phone continues sending newly captured encrypted DynamicDoxingData at intervals.
hnote over SAR #Pink:  Assert verify_payment(sar_service_fee_payment_receipts) == True
hnote over SAR #Pink:  Assert doxing_data_identifier == previously_received_doxing_data_identifier

' Step 7
SAR --> Phone:  <b>SetupSarPhoneMessage2 \n magic: "setup_sar_setup_done_and_in_sync_with_phone"
hnote over Phone #LavenderBlush:  Phone receives {magic: "setup_sar_setup_done_and_in_sync_with_phone"} from SAR and informs User that it's \n now in-sync with SAR.

' Step 8
Phone o-> User:  <b>SetupPhoneOutput2 \n magic: "setup_sar_registered_and_connected_to_phone"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "setup_sar_registered_and_connected_to_phone"} from Phone and proceeds to setup Iso.
end group
group Duress setup

' Step 9
User o-> Iso:  <b>SetupIsoInput1 \n network \n entropy_bytes \n passphrase \n doxing_password \n sar_id
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {network, entropy_bytes, passphrase, doxing_password, sar_id} from User. It creates mnemonic from entropy_bytes, derives master_xpriv_0 from that mnemonic and passphrase, \n and derives normal_privkey_0 as purpose_root_xpriv_0 at hardened path m/cb86', or m/52102h, where cb86 is the first two bytes of sha256("boomerang"). It derives normal_pubkey_0 from normal_privkey_0. \n Iso NFC-normalizes doxing_password and encodes it as UTF-8 bytes, then derives doxing_key as tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key", doxing_password_bytes) for installation into Boomlet. It retains \n mnemonic, passphrase, sar_id, and the derived normal-key material for the remainder of this Iso session.
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  mnemonic := mnemonic_from_entropy(entropy_bytes) \n master_xpriv_0 := derive_master_xpriv(mnemonic, passphrase) \n purpose_root_xpriv_0 := derive_hardened_child(master_xpriv_0, 52102) \n normal_privkey_0 := purpose_root_xpriv_0 \n normal_pubkey_0 := derive_public_key(normal_privkey_0) \n doxing_password_bytes := utf8(doxing_password) \n doxing_key := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key", doxing_password_bytes)

' Step 10
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupIsoBoomletMessage1 \n normal_pubkey_0 \n doxing_key \n sar_id
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {normal_pubkey_0, doxing_key, sar_id} from Iso during installation. It generates an identity private key and derives boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, \n generates a MuSig2 private share and derives its public share, and combines that public share with normal_pubkey_0 to derive boom_pubkey_0. Computing the aggregate key during installation validates the MuSig2 share and normal public key before setup continues. \n After successful installation on an empty smart card, Boomlet returns boomlet_0_identity_pubkey to Iso.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  boomlet_0_identity_privkey := generate_private_key() \n boomlet_0_boom_musig2_privkey_share := generate_private_key() \n boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share := derive_public_key(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_privkey_share) \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey := derive_public_key(boomlet_0_identity_privkey) \n boom_pubkey_0 := derive_musig2_public_key(boomlet_0_boom_musig2_pubkey_share, normal_pubkey_0)

' Step 11
Boomlet -> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletIsoMessage1 \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives boomlet_0_identity_pubkey from Boomlet and forwards it to ST.

' Step 12
Iso o-> ST:  <b>SetupIsoStMessage1 \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives boomlet_0_identity_pubkey from Iso, generates a new identity private key, derives st_0_identity_pubkey, retains the private key, and returns the public key.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  st_0_identity_privkey := generate_private_key() \n st_0_identity_pubkey := derive_public_key(st_0_identity_privkey)

' Step 13
ST o-> Iso:  <b>SetupStIsoMessage1 \n st_0_identity_pubkey
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives st_0_identity_pubkey from ST and forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 14
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupIsoBoomletMessage2 \n st_0_identity_pubkey
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives st_0_identity_pubkey from Iso. DuressCheckSpace contains one field, space, which Boomlet sets to a uniform random permutation of every integer from 1 through 193. \n MessageWithNonce contains content and nonce; Boomlet places the DuressCheckSpace in content and generates a fresh 32-byte nonce. It encrypts this value with the Boomlet-to-ST directional channel keys, using canonical context {"duress_challenge"}. \n The fresh nonce binds the eventual response to this exact challenge.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_check_space := DuressCheckSpace{space: random_permutation([1..193])} \n duress_check_space_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{\n content: duress_check_space \n nonce: random_bytes(32) } \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_challenge"),\n content: duress_check_space_with_nonce)

' Step 15
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletIsoMessage2 \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Boomlet and forwards it to ST.

' Step 16
Iso o-> ST:  <b>SetupIsoStMessage2 \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Iso and decrypts it with the Boomlet-to-ST directional channel keys, using canonical context {"duress_challenge"}. It takes DuressCheckSpace from the MessageWithNonce content, \n maps each integer through DURESS_DISPLAY_VOCABULARY, creates duress_display_columns as five independently shuffled display copies of that list, and retains the five corresponding \n display-to-original-index maps locally.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  duress_check_space_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_challenge"),\n envelope: duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st) \n duress_check_space := duress_check_space_with_nonce.content \n duress_display_columns, retained_display_maps := create_duress_display_columns(duress_check_space.space)

' Step 17
ST o-> User:  <b>SetupStOutput1 \n duress_display_columns
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives five independently shuffled columns of countries from ST and selects exactly one displayed country in each column with the joystick. \n This produces five displayed selections; ST will translate each one to an index in Boomlet's original list. User memorizes the five selected country names.
hnote over User #Lavender:  user_selection := select_one_from_each(duress_display_columns)

' Step 18
User o-> ST:  <b>SetupStInput1 \n user_selection
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives user_selection, containing exactly one displayed choice for each of the five columns, from User. It maps each choice through the corresponding retained display map to create \n duress_signal_index in column order. It places those five original-list indices in the content of a MessageWithNonce, copies the outstanding challenge nonce into the nonce field, \n and encrypts the response with the ST-to-Boomlet directional channel keys, using canonical context \n {"duress_response"}. It sends the resulting envelope to Iso.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  duress_signal_index := map_to_original_indices(user_selection, retained_display_maps) \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{\n content: duress_signal_index \n nonce: duress_check_space_with_nonce.nonce} \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_response"),\n content: duress_signal_index_with_nonce)

' Step 19
ST o-> Iso:  <b>SetupStIsoMessage2 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from ST and forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 20
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupIsoBoomletMessage3 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from Iso and decrypts it with the ST-to-Boomlet directional channel keys, using canonical context {"duress_response"}. It requires the returned nonce to equal the outstanding challenge nonce, \n takes the returned indices from content, resolves them against duress_check_space.space, and stores the resulting five integers as duress_consent_set. For confirmation it creates a new DuressCheckSpace from another permutation of 1 through 193, \n wraps it with a new random 32-byte nonce, and encrypts it with the Boomlet-to-ST directional channel keys, using canonical context \n {"duress_challenge"}.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_signal_index_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_response"),\n envelope: duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.nonce == duress_check_space_with_nonce.nonce
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert count(duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices) == 5 \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are distinct \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are in range [1..193]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_consent_set := duress_check_space.space[duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices]
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_check_space := DuressCheckSpace{space: random_permutation([1..193])} \n duress_check_space_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{\n content: duress_check_space \n nonce: random_bytes(32) } \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_challenge"),\n content: duress_check_space_with_nonce)

' Step 21
Boomlet -> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletIsoMessage3 \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Boomlet and forwards it to ST.

' Step 22
Iso o-> ST:  <b>SetupIsoStMessage3 \n duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Iso and decrypts it with the Boomlet-to-ST directional channel keys and canonical context \n {"duress_challenge"}. It extracts the new DuressCheckSpace and nonce, maps each integer through DURESS_DISPLAY_VOCABULARY, creates \n duress_display_columns as five independently shuffled display copies, and replaces retained_display_maps with their five display-to-original-index mappings for confirmation of duress_consent_set.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  duress_check_space_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_challenge"),\n envelope: duress_check_space_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st) \n duress_check_space := duress_check_space_with_nonce.content \n duress_display_columns, retained_display_maps := create_duress_display_columns(duress_check_space.space)

' Step 23
ST o-> User:  <b>SetupStOutput2 \n duress_display_columns
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives 5 independently shuffled columns from ST. He will select 1 country in each column to replicate the \n duress_consent_set and inputs it to ST.
hnote over User #Lavender:  user_selection := select_one_from_each(duress_display_columns)

' Step 24
User o-> ST:  <b>SetupStInput2 \n user_selection
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives user_selection, containing one displayed choice for each new column, from User. It maps the five choices through retained_display_maps to create duress_signal_index in column order \n and places those indices in MessageWithNonce content with the fresh challenge nonce. It encrypts the response with the ST-to-Boomlet directional channel keys and canonical context {"duress_response"}, then sends it to Iso.
hnote over ST #Pink:  Assert count(user_selection) == count(duress_display_columns) \n Assert count(user_selection) == 5 \n Assert user_selection contains exactly one displayed choice from each duress_display_columns column \n Assert each user_selection value exists in its corresponding duress_display_columns column
hnote over ST #Lavender:  duress_signal_index := map_to_original_indices(user_selection, retained_display_maps) \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{ \n content: duress_signal_index \n nonce: duress_check_space_with_nonce.nonce \n } \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_response"),\n content: duress_signal_index_with_nonce)
hnote over ST #Pink:  Assert count(duress_signal_index) == 5 \n Assert duress_signal_index values are distinct \n Assert duress_signal_index values are in range [1..193]

' Step 25
ST o-> Iso:  <b>SetupStIsoMessage3 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from ST and \n forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 26
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupIsoBoomletMessage4 \n duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from Iso and decrypts it with the ST-to-Boomlet directional channel keys and canonical context \n {"duress_response"}. It requires the returned nonce to equal the fresh outstanding nonce, extracts the indices, resolves them against the new \n duress_check_space.space, and requires the resulting five-element set to equal the stored duress_consent_set.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  duress_signal_index_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("duress_response"),\n envelope: duress_signal_index_with_nonce_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.nonce == duress_check_space_with_nonce.nonce
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert count(duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices) == 5 \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are distinct \n Assert duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices are in range [1..193]
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert duress_check_space.space[duress_signal_index_with_nonce.content.indices] == duress_consent_set

' Step 27
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletIsoMessage4 \n magic: "setup_duress_finished"
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {magic: "setup_duress_finished"} from Boomlet and knowing Boomlet can be disconnected, \n returns mnemonic to User.
end group
group Boomerang parameters setup

' Step 28
Iso o-> User:  <b>SetupIsoOutput1 \n mnemonic
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives mnemonic from Iso, saves it in a safe place and proceeds to shutdown Iso and connect Boomlet \n to Niso to continue setup.

' Step 29
User o-> Niso:  <b>SetupNisoInput1 \n network \n rpc_client_url \n rpc_client_auth
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {network, rpc_client_url, rpc_client_auth} from User during the installation. rpc_client_url \n and rpc_client_auth provide a direct view into the provided network. As Niso communicates through TOR, \n Niso asks for peer_0_tor_secret_key from Boomlet.

' Step 30
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupNisoBoomletMessage1 \n magic: "setup_initialized"
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {magic: "setup_initialized"} from Niso, generates peer_0_tor_secret_key and a fresh 32-byte peer_0_setup_nonce, and derives peer_0_tor_address from the Tor secret key. \n It creates PeerId containing boom_pubkey_0, normal_pubkey_0, and boomlet_0_identity_pubkey. PeerSetupRecord contains peer_0_id, peer_0_setup_nonce, and peer_0_tor_address. \n Boomlet signs the record with boomlet_0_identity_privkey under domain "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record"; `PROTOCOL_VERSION` is bound by the signature context. sign_message produces a SignedMessage containing the signer identity public key, domain, content, and signature. \n Boomlet returns the signed record and Tor secret key to Niso. The authenticated record is the only transmitted carrier of peer_0_id and peer_0_setup_nonce.
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  peer_0_tor_secret_key := generate_private_key() \n peer_0_setup_nonce := random_bytes(32) \n peer_0_tor_address := derive_tor_address(peer_0_tor_secret_key) \n peer_0_id := PeerId{ \n boom_pubkey: boom_pubkey_0, \n normal_pubkey: normal_pubkey_0, \n boomlet_identity_pubkey: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n} \n peer_0_setup_identity_record := PeerSetupRecord{peer_id: peer_0_id, peer_setup_nonce: peer_0_setup_nonce, tor_address: peer_0_tor_address} \n peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record", peer_0_setup_identity_record)

' Step 31
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>SetupBoomletNisoMessage1 \n peer_0_tor_secret_key \n peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {peer_0_tor_secret_key, peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0} from Boomlet, extracts peer_0_id from the signed record, and verifies domain \n "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record" using the Boomlet identity public key inside that PeerId. It derives peer_0_tor_address from peer_0_tor_secret_key, requires it to equal the record's tor_address, and forwards only the signed record to ST.
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0.content.peer_id.boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record", peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0) == True
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  peer_0_tor_address := derive_tor_address(peer_0_tor_secret_key).
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0.content.tor_address == peer_0_tor_address.

' Step 32
Niso o-> ST:  <b>SetupNisoStMessage1 \n peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives the signed setup identity record. Since ST already knows boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, it checks that the record contains the same identity pubkey.
hnote over ST #Pink:  Assert peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0.content.peer_id.boomlet_identity_pubkey == boomlet_0_identity_pubkey

' Step 33
ST o-> User:  <b>SetupStOutput3 \n peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives the signed setup identity record and shares it with peers over the secure out-of-band channel.

' Step 34
User <--> Peers:  <b>SetupUserPeersOutOfBandMessage1 \n peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i for peer indices 1 through 4 from Peers while sending peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0. \n User forms peer_setup_records_collection from exactly five signed PeerSetupRecord values, one for each peer indexed 0 through 4, and also supplies milestone_block_collection and the preference-ordered wt_ids_collection. \n Each WtId contains a WT Tor address and WT public key.
hnote over User #Lavender:  peer_setup_records_collection := Collection<peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i> [0 <= i <= 4]

' Step 35
User o-> Niso:  <b>SetupNisoInput2 \n peer_setup_records_collection \n wt_ids_collection \n milestone_block_collection
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {peer_setup_records_collection, wt_ids_collection, milestone_block_collection} from User. The User-to-Niso peer-record collection may be unordered. For every peer index 0 through 4 it verifies domain \n "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record" using the Boomlet identity key inside the record, then connects to peers 1 through 4 at the Tor addresses authenticated by their records. It requires its own exact signed record \n to occur exactly once in the collection. Niso sorts the five records by encoded Boomlet identity public-key bytes into ordered_peer_setup_records. Niso selects the first WtId in the preference-ordered wt_ids_collection as active_wt_id and takes wt_pubkey from that WtId before forwarding ordered_peer_setup_records, WtIds, and milestones to Boomlet.
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i.content.peer_id.boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record", peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4].
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  Connect to peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i.content.tor_address [1 <= i <= 4]. \n ordered_peer_setup_records := peer_setup_records_collection sorted by encoded Boomlet identity pubkey \n active_wt_id := wt_ids_collection[0] \n wt_pubkey := active_wt_id.wt_pubkey
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0 is included exactly once in peer_setup_records_collection.

' Step 36
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupNisoBoomletMessage2 \n ordered_peer_setup_records \n wt_ids_collection \n milestone_block_collection
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {ordered_peer_setup_records, wt_ids_collection, milestone_block_collection} from Niso. It verifies strictly increasing identity-key encodings, rejects duplicates, verifies domain \n "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record" using the identity key in each record and the protocol-version signature context, and requires its own exact signed record to occur once. It extracts \n peer_ids_collection and ordered Boomlet identity keys in that same order while constructing or incrementally hashing BoomerangParamsSeed. It selects the first WtId in preference order as active_wt_id and takes wt_pubkey from it. \n BoomerangParamsSeed contains the identity-key-ordered signed peer records, the preference-ordered WtIds, and milestone blocks accepted from Niso. Boomlet computes setup_instance_id as the tagged hash of `PROTOCOL_VERSION` and canonical BoomerangParamsSeed. \n It places setup_instance_id in MessageWithNonce content with a fresh 32-byte nonce, then encrypts it with the Boomlet-to-ST directional channel keys, using canonical context \n {"params_review", setup_instance_id}. It sends the outer setup ID and encrypted setup-ID envelope to Niso.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i.content.peer_id.boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/peer_setup_record", peer_i_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [0 <= i <= 4].
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert peer_0_setup_identity_record_signed_by_boomlet_0 is included exactly once in ordered_peer_setup_records.
group ST review of BoomerangParamsSeed commitment
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert ordered_peer_setup_records are strictly increasing by encoded Boomlet identity pubkey
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  peer_ids_collection := Collection<ordered_peer_setup_records.content.peer_id> [0 <= i <= 4] \n ordered_boomlet_identity_pubkeys := Collection<ordered_peer_setup_records.content.peer_id.boomlet_identity_pubkey> [0 <= i <= 4] \n active_wt_id := wt_ids_collection[0] \n wt_pubkey := active_wt_id.wt_pubkey \n boomerang_params_seed := BoomerangParamsSeed{ordered_peer_setup_records: ordered_peer_setup_records, wt_ids: wt_ids_collection, milestone_blocks: milestone_block_collection} \n setup_instance_id := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/setup_instance_id", canonical_encode(PROTOCOL_VERSION, boomerang_params_seed)) \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce := MessageWithNonce{ \n content: setup_instance_id \n nonce: random_bytes(32) \n} \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("params_review", setup_instance_id),\n content: setup_instance_id_with_nonce)

' Step 37
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>SetupBoomletNisoMessage2 \n setup_instance_id \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives setup_instance_id and setup_instance_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st from Boomlet. It forwards both to ST together with the ordered seed fields it already sent to Boomlet. \n The setup ID is required to construct the encrypt-then-MAC context and is authenticated by the envelope CMAC.

' Step 38
Niso o-> ST:  <b>SetupNisoStMessage2 \n setup_instance_id \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st \n ordered_peer_setup_records \n wt_ids_collection \n milestone_block_collection
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives setup_instance_id, the encrypted nonce-bound setup ID, and ordered seed fields from Niso. It decrypts the setup ID with the Boomlet-to-ST directional channel keys, using canonical context {"params_review", setup_instance_id}. \n It constructs BoomerangParamsSeed from the ordered fields, rejects malformed encodings, duplicate or non-increasing identity-key order, and non-canonical seed fields before display. It recomputes setup_instance_id from the constructed seed and requires it to match the decrypted nonce-bound setup ID and outer setup ID. \n Only after that match does ST show the ordered fields to User while retaining the nonce-bound setup ID for approval.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  setup_instance_id_with_nonce := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("params_review", setup_instance_id),\n envelope: setup_instance_id_with_nonce_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_st) \n decrypted_setup_instance_id := setup_instance_id_with_nonce.content \n boomerang_params_seed := BoomerangParamsSeed{ordered_peer_setup_records: ordered_peer_setup_records, wt_ids: wt_ids_collection, milestone_blocks: milestone_block_collection} \n recomputed_setup_instance_id := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/setup_instance_id", canonical_encode(PROTOCOL_VERSION, boomerang_params_seed))
hnote over ST #Pink:  Assert decrypted_setup_instance_id == setup_instance_id
hnote over ST #Pink:  Assert ordered_peer_setup_records are strictly increasing by encoded Boomlet identity pubkey
hnote over ST #Pink:  Assert decrypted_setup_instance_id == recomputed_setup_instance_id

' Step 39
ST o-> User:  <b>SetupStOutput4 \n ordered_peer_setup_records \n wt_ids_collection \n milestone_block_collection
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives the ordered seed fields from ST after ST has matched them against Boomlet's encrypted nonce-bound setup ID. User requires the ordered signed peer records to equal the expected sorted collection, the ordered WtIds to equal the selected WT \n preference order, and the milestones to equal milestone_block_collection. User approves only if every displayed field matches the values intended for BoomerangParams review.
hnote over User #Lavender:  expected_ordered_peer_setup_records := peer_setup_records_collection sorted by encoded Boomlet identity pubkey
hnote over User #Pink:  Assert ordered_peer_setup_records == expected_ordered_peer_setup_records
hnote over User #Pink:  Assert displayed wt_ids_collection == intended wt_ids_collection
hnote over User #Pink:  Assert displayed milestone_block_collection == intended milestone_block_collection

' Step 40
User o-> ST:  <b>SetupStInput3 \n magic: "setup_user_verified_peer_ids_and_wt_ids_received_with_those_registered_before"
hnote over ST #LavenderBlush:  ST receives {magic: "setup_user_verified_peer_ids_and_wt_ids_received_with_those_registered_before"} from User and signs the exact retained setup_instance_id_with_nonce \n under domain "Boomerang/setup/params_review_approval". It encrypts that SignedMessage with the ST-to-Boomlet directional channel keys, using canonical context {"params_review_approval", setup_instance_id}, then sends the envelope to Niso.
hnote over ST #Lavender:  setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st := sign_message(st_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/setup/params_review_approval", setup_instance_id_with_nonce) \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(st_0_identity_privkey, "st", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("params_review_approval", setup_instance_id),\n content: setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st)

' Step 41
ST o-> Niso:  <b>SetupStNisoMessage1 \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from ST \n and forwards it to Boomlet.

' Step 42
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupNisoBoomletMessage3 \n setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0 from Niso and decrypts it with the ST-to-Boomlet directional channel keys, using canonical context {"params_review_approval", setup_instance_id}. \n It verifies ST's signature under that same domain and requires the signed MessageWithNonce, including nonce, to equal the outstanding setup_instance_id_with_nonce value. It constructs boomerang_descriptor from ordered peer_ids_collection and \n milestone_block_collection. BoomerangParams contains setup_instance_id, ordered peer IDs, ordered WtIds, milestone blocks, and boomerang_descriptor; the full BoomerangParamsSeed is not retained in it. Boomlet computes \n boomerang_params_fingerprint as tagged_sha256("Boomerang/boomerang_params", canonical BoomerangParams) and signs that 32-byte fingerprint with boomlet_0_identity_privkey under domain "Boomerang/setup/agreement".
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "boomlet", st_0_identity_pubkey, "st", sender_public_key: st_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("params_review_approval", setup_instance_id),\n envelope: setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st_encrypted_by_st_for_boomlet_0)
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(st_0_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/params_review_approval", setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Freshness Check \n Assert setup_instance_id_with_nonce_signed_by_st.content == setup_instance_id_with_nonce
end group
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  boomerang_descriptor := construct_boomerang_descriptor(peer_ids_collection, milestone_block_collection) \n boomerang_params := BoomerangParams{ \n setup_instance_id: setup_instance_id, \n peer_ids: peer_ids_collection, \n wt_ids: wt_ids_collection, \n milestone_blocks: milestone_block_collection, \n boomerang_descriptor: boomerang_descriptor \n} \n boomerang_params_fingerprint := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/boomerang_params", canonical_encode(boomerang_params)) \n boomerang_params_fingerprint_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/setup/agreement", boomerang_params_fingerprint)
