' Step 78
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletIsoMessage5 \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n boomlet_0_backup_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomletwo \n boomerang_params \n sar_setup_response_signed_by_sar
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, boomlet_0_backup_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomletwo, boomerang_params, sar_setup_response_signed_by_sar} from Boomlet. It requires \n boomerang_params.milestone_blocks to equal milestone_block_collection, reconstructs boomerang_descriptor from boomerang_params.peer_ids and boomerang_params.milestone_blocks, and requires equality with \n boomerang_params.boomerang_descriptor. It also requires boomlet_0_identity_pubkey to appear exactly once in boomerang_params.peer_ids. It uses local network configuration for network-specific display and validation. \n It NFC-normalizes doxing_password and encodes it as UTF-8 bytes, derives doxing_key as tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key", doxing_password_bytes), extracts sar_pubkey from the signed response's signer identity, \n obtains its canonical public-key bytes, derives doxing_key_for_sar as tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key_for_sar", doxing_key || sar_pubkey_bytes), and derives doxing_data_identifier as \n tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_data_identifier", doxing_key_for_sar). It verifies the SAR signature under "Boomerang/setup/sar_response", requires the response setup_instance_id to equal \n boomerang_params.setup_instance_id and its identifier to equal the derived value. Using keys derived from doxing_key_for_sar and "Boomerang/sar_stored_data", context {"sar_static_data", doxing_data_identifier}, \n the user's static data, and the response IV, Iso recreates the static-data envelope and requires its sha256 to equal the response fingerprint.
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert boomerang_params.milestone_blocks == milestone_block_collection
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  boomerang_descriptor := construct_boomerang_descriptor(boomerang_params.peer_ids, boomerang_params.milestone_blocks)
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert boomerang_descriptor == boomerang_params.boomerang_descriptor
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert count(boomerang_params.peer_ids, boomlet_0_identity_pubkey) == 1
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  doxing_password_bytes := utf8(doxing_password) \n doxing_key := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key", doxing_password_bytes) \n sar_pubkey := sar_setup_response_signed_by_sar.signer_identity_pubkey \n sar_pubkey_bytes := canonical_public_key_bytes(sar_pubkey) \n doxing_key_for_sar := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_key_for_sar", doxing_key || sar_pubkey_bytes) \n doxing_data_identifier := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_data_identifier", doxing_key_for_sar)
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(sar_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/sar_response", sar_setup_response_signed_by_sar) == True
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  sar_setup_response := sar_setup_response_signed_by_sar.content
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert sar_setup_response.setup_instance_id == boomerang_params.setup_instance_id
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert sar_setup_response.doxing_data_identifier == doxing_data_identifier
hnote over Iso #Lavender:  recreated_static_doxing_ciphertext := cbc_cmac_encrypt(\n keys: derive_cbc_cmac_keys(doxing_key_for_sar, "Boomerang/sar_stored_data"),\n context: canonical_encode("sar_static_data", doxing_data_identifier),\n content: static_doxing_data,\n iv: sar_setup_response.iv_of_static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar)
hnote over Iso #Pink:  Assert sar_setup_response.fingerprint_of_static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar == sha256(recreated_static_doxing_ciphertext)

' Step 79
Iso o-> User:  <b>SetupIsoOutput3 \n magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_data_received_connect_boomletwo_to_iso"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_data_received_connect_boomletwo_to_iso"} from Iso. User then \n proceeds to connect Boomletwo to Iso.

' Step 80
User o-> Iso:  <b>SetupIsoInput4 \n magic: "setup_user_is_asked_to_connect_boomletwo_to_iso_boomletwo_connected_to_iso"
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {magic: "setup_user_is_asked_to_connect_boomletwo_to_iso_boomletwo_connected_to_iso"} from User \n and proceeds to give the backup file to Boomletwo.

' Step 81
Iso o-> Boomletwo:  <b>SetupIsoBoomletwo2 \n boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n boomlet_0_backup_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomletwo
hnote over Boomletwo #LavenderBlush:  Boomletwo receives {boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, boomlet_0_backup_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomletwo} from Iso and first requires its memory to be empty. It decrypts BoomletBackupState \n with the Boomlet-to-Boomletwo directional channel keys, using canonical context \n {"backup_state"}. It takes setup_instance_id from the authenticated state and imports every state field. It draws its own mystery uniformly and inclusively between \n MIN_TRIES_FOR_DIGGING_GAME_IN_BLOCKS and MAX_TRIES_FOR_DIGGING_GAME_IN_BLOCKS. BackupDone contains the imported setup_instance_id, backup_boomlet_pubkey set to boomletwo_Identity_pubkey, \n and boomlet_pubkey set to boomlet_0_identity_pubkey. Boomletwo signs it with boomletwo_Identity_privkey under domain "Boomerang/setup/backup_done".
hnote over Boomletwo #Pink:  Assert boomletwo.memory is empty
hnote over Boomletwo #Lavender:  boomlet_backup_state := cbc_cmac_decrypt(\n keys: channel_keys(boomletwo_Identity_privkey, "boomletwo", boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, "boomlet", sender_public_key: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey, receiver_public_key: boomletwo_Identity_pubkey),\n context: canonical_encode("backup_state"),\n envelope: boomlet_0_backup_encrypted_by_boomlet_0_for_boomletwo) \n setup_instance_id := boomlet_backup_state.setup_instance_id \n boomletwo.memory += boomlet_backup_state \n mystery := random_integer(MIN_TRIES_FOR_DIGGING_GAME_IN_BLOCKS, MAX_TRIES_FOR_DIGGING_GAME_IN_BLOCKS) \n backup_done := BackupDone{\n setup_instance_id: setup_instance_id, \n backup_boomlet_pubkey: boomletwo_Identity_pubkey, \n boomlet_pubkey: boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n}\n backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo := sign_message(boomletwo_Identity_privkey, "Boomerang/setup/backup_done", backup_done)

' Step 82
Boomletwo o-> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletwoIso2 \n backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo} from Boomletwo. Iso proceeds to inform User to connect Boomlet.

' Step 83
Iso o-> User:  <b>SetupIsoOutput4 \n magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_done_connect_boomlet_to_iso"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_done_connect_boomlet_to_iso"} from Iso and connects Boomlet to Iso.

' Step 84
User o-> Iso:  <b>SetupIsoInput5 \n magic: "setup_user_is_asked_to_connect_boomlet_to_iso_boomlet_connected_to_iso"
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {magic: "setup_user_is_asked_to_connect_boomlet_to_iso_boomlet_connected_to_iso"} from User \n and proceeds to forward backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo to Boomlet.

' Step 85
Iso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupIsoBoomletMessage6 \n backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo from Iso and verifies boomletwo_Identity_pubkey's signature under domain "Boomerang/setup/backup_done". \n It extracts BackupDone and requires setup_instance_id equal to the active setup ID, backup_boomlet_pubkey equal to boomletwo_Identity_pubkey, and boomlet_pubkey equal to boomlet_0_identity_pubkey. \n Once accepted it marks backup complete and will not accept another backup request for this active state.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomletwo_Identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/backup_done", backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo) == True
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  backup_done := backup_done_signed_by_boomletwo.content
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert backup_done.setup_instance_id == setup_instance_id
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert backup_done.backup_boomlet_pubkey == boomletwo_Identity_pubkey
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert backup_done.boomlet_pubkey == boomlet_0_identity_pubkey \n backup_complete := True

' Step 86
Boomlet o-> Iso:  <b>SetupBoomletIsoMessage6 \n magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_done"
hnote over Iso #LavenderBlush:  Iso receives {magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_done"} from Boomlet and proceeds to inform User that the \n backup process has been completed.

' Step 87
Iso o-> User:  <b>SetupIsoOutput5 \n magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_completed_boomlet_closed_ready_to_finish_setup"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "setup_boomlet_backup_completed_boomlet_closed_ready_to_finish_setup"} from Iso. \n User proceeds to connect Boomlet to Niso.

' Step 88
User o-> Niso:  <b>SetupNisoInput4 \n magic: "setup_user_is_informed_that_boomlet_is_closed"
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {magic: "setup_user_is_informed_that_boomlet_is_closed"} from User and proceeds to tell Boomlet to finish the setup procedure.

' Step 89
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupNisoBoomletMessage11 \n magic: "setup_boomlet_closed_finish_setup"
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives {magic: "setup_boomlet_closed_finish_setup"} from Niso. Because it already verified BackupDone locally, it updates setup_checkpoint from setup_instance_id, \n phase "backup_ready", and previous setup_checkpoint and signs it with boomlet_0_identity_privkey under domain "Boomerang/setup/phase_checkpoint". The peer-specific BackupDone receipt is not hashed into setup_checkpoint.
group Backup-ready checkpoint synchronization
hnote over Boomlet #Lavender:  setup_checkpoint := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/setup_phase_checkpoint", canonical_encode(setup_instance_id, "backup_ready", setup_checkpoint)) \n setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_0 := sign_message(boomlet_0_identity_privkey, "Boomerang/setup/phase_checkpoint", setup_checkpoint)

' Step 90 - Step 1
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>SetupBoomletNisoMessage11 \n setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_0
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_0 and shares it with Peers.

' Step 91 - Step 2
Niso <-> Peers:  <b>SetupNisoPeerNisoMessage4 \n setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i [0 <= i <= 4]
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i for peer indices 1 through 4 from Peers while sharing its local signed checkpoint. It verifies each peer signature under domain \n "Boomerang/setup/phase_checkpoint", requires each signed content value to equal setup_checkpoint, and forms setup_checkpoint_signed_by_all_peers from those four peer values.
hnote over Niso #Lavender:  setup_checkpoint := setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_0.content
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_setup_records_collection[i].content.peer_id.boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/phase_checkpoint", setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [1 <= i <= 4].
hnote over Niso #Pink:  Assert setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i.content == setup_checkpoint [1 <= i <= 4] \n setup_checkpoint_signed_by_all_peers := Collection<setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i> [1 <= i <= 4]

' Step 92 - Step 3
Niso o-> Boomlet:  <b>SetupNisoBoomletMessage12 \n setup_checkpoint_signed_by_all_peers: Collection<setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i>
hnote over Boomlet #LavenderBlush:  Boomlet receives setup_checkpoint_signed_by_all_peers, a collection for peer indices 1 through 4, from Niso. It verifies each peer signature under domain \n "Boomerang/setup/phase_checkpoint" and requires every signed content value to equal setup_checkpoint. It persists setup_checkpoint as its local final setup_checkpoint and finishes setup only after all four peer checks succeed.
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(peer_ids_collection[i].boomlet_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/setup/phase_checkpoint", setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i) == True [1 <= i <= 4].
hnote over Boomlet #Pink:  Assert setup_checkpoint_signed_by_boomlet_i.content == setup_checkpoint [1 <= i <= 4] \n final_setup_checkpoint := setup_checkpoint \n Commit final_setup_checkpoint to durable Boomlet storage before reporting setup success.
end

' Step 93
Boomlet o-> Niso:  <b>SetupBoomletNisoMessage12 \n magic: "setup_done"
hnote over Niso #LavenderBlush:  Niso receives {magic: "setup_done"} from Boomlet and proceeds to inform User that setup is finished. \n setup_instance_id is already part of the agreed setup state, and the final `setup_checkpoint` remains local to Boomlet.

' Step 94
Niso o-> User:  <b>SetupNisoOutput3 \n magic: "setup_done"
hnote over User #LavenderBlush:  User receives {magic: "setup_done"} from Niso.
end group

@enduml
